["flow d68c82 seats: Fable judges; lower layers shovel (2026-10-13)" "I'd also like to talk about how we can insulate Fable from the low-level drudgery, the shoveling aspect that should be the concern of lower levels.\n\nI see a world where we have Fable Flow, or more than one, which doesn't actually have hardly any tool access. Something like that, where any questions that it brings forth would be researched and answered by other models. Some hooks would automatically forward these questions. The Fable Flow wouldn't have to make the call to a sub-agent to look into stuff. It would just pose the question and the question would be answered. The answer would be given back to it the next time it gets a turn, with all the other things that would be queued for it: whether they're new insights from the psyche, information that a previous turn was asking about, or anything like that. All of its context would revolve around making judgments, inferring, and summarizing instead of actually grabbing the shovel handle and shoveling."]
